{"name":"Ponzu Brown","hex":"#220000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ponzu","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sour citrus-based sauce usually made from the juice of the 橙 (daidai), an Asian variety of bitter orange, mixed with soy sauce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ponzu"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ponzu","blocks":[{"text":"Ponzu (ポン酢) is a citrus-based sauce commonly used in Japanese cuisine. It is tart, with a thin, watery consistency. Ponzu shōyu or ponzu jōyu (ポン酢醤油) is ponzu with soy sauce added, and the mixed dark brown product is widely referred to as simply ponzu."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Canada_Prime_Beef_Tataki_with_ponzu_pearls_and_horseradish_%285895881268%29.jpg/330px-Canada_Prime_Beef_Tataki_with_ponzu_pearls_and_horseradish_%285895881268%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponzu","wikidata":"Q2722814"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/%E3%81%BD%E3%82%93%E9%85%A2.jpg/500px-%E3%81%BD%E3%82%93%E9%85%A2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa